  "id": "amantadine",
  "term": "amantadine",
  "definition": "Amantadine is a drug used to help prevent or relieve influenza A and is also used in movement-related conditions such as Parkinsonian symptoms, extrapyramidal reactions, and postherpetic neuralgia. Its effects on movement problems are not fully understood, but they may involve increasing dopamine production and release and possibly reducing dopamine uptake.",
